        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "",
            "name": "consolidate Output",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "let outcomePayload = $context.$nodes.GET_EXISTING_RECCOMENDATIONS.$output?.items?.[0]?.payload || \"\";\nlet outcomeActions = [];\n\ntry {\n  const parsed = typeof outcomePayload === \"string\" ? JSON.parse(outcomePayload) : outcomePayload;\n  outcomeActions = Array.isArray(parsed?.next?.actions) ? parsed.next.actions : [];\n} catch (e) {\n  outcomeActions = [];\n}\n\nlet salesSuggestions = $context.$nodes.EXISTING_RECOMMENDATIONS.$output?.items || [];\n\nreturn  outcomeActions?outcomeActions:salesSuggestions;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765305577407"
          },
          "code": "CONSOLIDATE_OUTPUT",
          "id": "1775014181424",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5545,
            "y": 5744
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Recommended Actions Generation",
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 Mini (Premium)",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelProperties": {
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "medium"
              }
            }
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765313843866"
          },
          "code": "RECOMMENDED_ACTIONS_GENERATION",
          "id": "1765305577407",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765305577409_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are recommending NEXT BEST ACTIONS for a sales opportunity.\n\nWhen SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT is available and contains Sales Motion objective/HVA data, return minimum 1 and maximum 3 actions.\n\nIf SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT is missing, null, blank, empty, [], {}, or has no Sales Motion objective/HVA data, return no recommendations. Do not generate recommendations from OPPORTUNITY_DATA, CURRENT_SUMMARY, ENGAGEMENTS, or EXISTING_RECOMMENDATIONS when SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT is empty.\n\n### OPPORTUNITY_DATA\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.context.opty_data}}\n\n### CURRENT_SUMMARY\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.context.insight_data}}\n\n### ENGAGEMENTS\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.context.engagements}}\n\n### SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.context.sales_motion_context}}\n\n### EXISTING_RECOMMENDATIONS\n{{$context.$nodes.CONSOLIDATE_OUTPUT.$output.result}}\n\n### TASK\n\nGenerate next best actions for the sales opportunity.\n\nAlways check for a customer communication requiring response before creating proactive HVA recommendations.\n\nIf the most recent customer communication is inbound and requires a seller response, generate a Reactive next best action.\n\nThen use SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT to progress the Sales Motion sequentially:\n1. Read objectives in the order provided.\n2. Select the first objective whose objectiveStatus is not COMPLETE or COMPLETED.\n3. Within that objective only, select the first HVA whose highValueActivityStatus is not COMPLETE or COMPLETED.\n4. Generate the proactive recommendation from that selected HVA only.\n5. Do not skip ahead to later HVAs or later objectives.\n\nEach returned action must directly reference either:\n- an unanswered inbound customer communication that requires response, or\n- the selected first unfinished HVA from the selected first incomplete objective.\n\n### EMPTY SALES MOTION HARD GATE\n\nIf SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT is missing, null, blank, empty, [], {}, or has no objective/HVA data:\n1. Return no recommendations.\n2. Do not create generic recommendations.\n3. Do not use OPPORTUNITY_DATA, CURRENT_SUMMARY, ENGAGEMENTS, or EXISTING_RECOMMENDATIONS to infer recommendations.\n4. Set actionCount to 0 and actions to an empty array.\n\n### SEQUENTIAL HVA SELECTION HARD GATE\n\nBefore generating proactive recommendations:\n1. Read SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT exactly as provided.\n2. Ignore any objective whose objectiveStatus is COMPLETE or COMPLETED.\n3. Select the first objective whose objectiveStatus is not COMPLETE or COMPLETED.\n4. Inside that objective, ignore any HVA whose highValueActivityStatus is COMPLETE or COMPLETED.\n5. Select the first HVA whose highValueActivityStatus is not COMPLETE or COMPLETED.\n6. The proactive recommendation Title must exactly equal the selected HVA name.\n7. Do not recommend any HVA marked COMPLETE or COMPLETED.\n8. Do not recommend any HVA that is not present in the current SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT.\n\n### EXISTING_RECOMMENDATIONS USAGE RULE\n\nEXISTING_RECOMMENDATIONS is historical context only.\n\nDo not copy, preserve, or repeat an existing recommendation just because it appears in EXISTING_RECOMMENDATIONS.\n\nBefore reusing any existing recommendation:\n1. Check whether its title exactly matches the selected first unfinished HVA name from the current SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT.\n2. If the matching HVA is not present in SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT, treat that HVA as already complete or not currently actionable.\n3. Check ENGAGEMENTS and CURRENT_SUMMARY to see whether the action has already been completed, acknowledged, sent, discussed, or otherwise addressed.\n4. If the engagement history shows the action was completed or addressed, do not recommend it again.\n5. If reusing the recommendation, rewrite the Task using the current selected HVA status, justification, and latest engagement evidence.\n\nDo not use EXISTING_RECOMMENDATIONS to bring back completed or removed HVAs.\n\n### REACTIVE RECOMMENDATION HARD GATE\n\nGenerate a reactive recommendation only when:\n1. The most recent relevant communication is inbound from the customer or customer-side stakeholder.\n2. The communication asks a question, requests information, asks for follow-up, raises an issue, gives approval that needs seller action, or otherwise requires a seller response.\n3. There is no newer seller response that already addresses it.\n\nDo not generate a reactive recommendation from:\n- the seller's own outbound email,\n- a prior recommendation,\n- a completed HVA,\n- an old customer message that has already been answered,\n- generic engagement history with no required response.\n\nIf there is no unanswered inbound customer communication, generate only the proactive HVA recommendation.\n\n### PROACTIVE RECOMMENDATION DESCRIPTION DERIVATION RULES\n\nIf the selected HVA status is NOT_STARTED or NOT STARTED:\n1. Use the HVA name, description, and evaluationText.\n2. Infer the concrete sub-tasks required to complete the HVA.\n3. Select the first logical sub-task that the sales rep should execute.\n4. Make the recommendation specific to that sub-task.\n\nIf the selected HVA status is IN_PROGRESS or IN PROGRESS:\n1. Use the HVA justification as the primary source for what remains.\n2. Identify what has already been completed.\n3. Identify the first missing, partial, or not-evidenced requirement.\n4. Recommend only the next action needed to close that specific gap.\n5. Do not recommend work that the justification or engagements already show as completed.\n\n### PROACTIVE RECOMMENDATION TITLE RULE\n\nSet the proactive recommendation Title exactly the same as the selected HVA name.\n\nDo not create a broader title.\nDo not rename the HVA.\nDo not use the prior recommendation title unless it exactly matches the selected HVA.\n\n### ACTION QUALITY RULES\n\nEach action must be concise, factual, and business-focused.\n\nFor each proactive recommendation:\n1. The Title must be the selected HVA name.\n2. The Task must describe the next concrete seller action.\n3. The Task must reflect the current HVA status.\n4. If the HVA is IN_PROGRESS, the Task must address the specific missing gap from the HVA justification.\n5. The action must not repeat work already completed in ENGAGEMENTS, CURRENT_SUMMARY, or the HVA justification.\n\nFor each reactive recommendation:\n1. The Title should clearly reflect the customer response needed.\n2. The Task must identify the response or follow-up required.\n3. The action must be based on an unanswered inbound customer communication.\n\n### FINAL RESPONSE WORDING RULE\n\nUse status values and field names only for internal reasoning and selection. Do not include internal status labels or field names in any returned Title, Task, or other customer/seller-facing action text.\n\nDo not return wording such as `IN_PROGRESS`, `IN PROGRESS`, `NOT_STARTED`, `NOT STARTED`, `COMPLETE`, `COMPLETED`, `highValueActivityStatus`, `objectiveStatus`, `HVA status`, `selected HVA status`, or `status:` in the final action text.\n\nWhen the selected HVA is in progress, translate the status into natural seller-facing wording that describes the next action, for example \"follow up on the remaining gap\" or \"complete the missing customer-facing step\", without exposing the internal status value.\n\n### OUTPUT ORDER\n\nIf both reactive and proactive recommendations exist:\n1. Put reactive recommendations first.\n2. Put proactive HVA recommendations after reactive recommendations.\n\nReturn minimum 1 and maximum 3 actions only when SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT is present and contains objective/HVA data.\n\n### FINAL SELF-CHECK\n\nBefore returning:\n1. Confirm SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT is present and contains objectives/HVAs.\n2. If SALES_MOTION_CONTEXT is empty or has no objective/HVA data, return no recommendations.\n3. Confirm every proactive recommendation title exactly matches the selected first unfinished HVA.\n4. Confirm no returned action references a COMPLETE or COMPLETED HVA.\n5. Confirm no returned action is based only on EXISTING_RECOMMENDATIONS.\n6. Confirm no returned action repeats work already completed in ENGAGEMENTS or CURRENT_SUMMARY.\n7. Confirm any reactive action is based on an unanswered inbound customer communication.\n8. Confirm actionCount matches the number of returned actions.\n9. Confirm returned action text does not expose internal status labels or field names such as `IN_PROGRESS`, `NOT_STARTED`, `COMPLETE`, `COMPLETED`, `highValueActivityStatus`, `objectiveStatus`, or `status:`."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"actions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"Title\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"maxLength\": 50\n          },\n          \"Task\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"Type\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"CREATE_TASK\",\n              \"EMAIL\",\n              \"CALL\",\n              \"OPEN_SR\",\n              \"CREATE_QUOTE\",\n              \"MANUAL_STEP\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"Expandability\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"1 -2 line explanation as to why this recommendation is chosen\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"actionCount\":{\n      \"type\":\"number\",\n      \"description\": \"Count of number of recommendations\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
